# Airtulip — DO NOT push or deploy themes (agent hard stop)

## Absolute rule — read every session

**The developer owns ALL Shopify CLI deploy operations.** The agent must **NEVER**:

- Run **`shopify theme push`** (any flags: `--live`, `--allow-live`, `-d`, `--development`, `--only`, `--theme=`, etc.)
- Run **`shopify theme pull`**
- Run **`shopify theme dev`**, **`npm run dev`**, or **`npm run storefront`**
- Run **`shopify theme publish`**
- Run **`shopify theme delete`**, **`shopify theme duplicate`**, or any command that **writes to a remote Shopify theme**
- Push to the **live / published** theme under any circumstances unless the user gives an **explicit one-time written exception** naming the exact theme ID and command

**Local Git edits only.** The developer runs terminal push/pull and uses **local preview** (`shopify theme dev`) to verify. The agent edits files in this repo and stops there.

## Why this exists

Pushing to the wrong theme — especially the **live** storefront theme — can change what customers see immediately. That is never the agent’s job on this project.

## What agents SHOULD do instead

- Edit Liquid, JSON templates, `assets/`, `config/`, etc. in the repo
- Tell the developer which files changed and what to push when they are ready
- If verification is needed, describe what to check in **their** local preview URL — do not start the dev server yourself unless explicitly asked

